// ======== foldSlot: a band of the surface folded into a wedge along a path ========
//
// An undercut groove with a crisp opening (the knight's mouth slit, an eyelid slit) laid on a surface that is
// otherwise a height field, as ONE surface: no boolean, no second mesh, no seam. The surface is built with the slot
// CLOSED (each cut runs straight across the mouth, so the opening is a flat chord); foldSlot then moves the opening's
// vertices into the wedge. This is how the 27 Nov 2026 front-strip experiment made the slit: the chord's vertices were
// moved into the triangle given by three tracks (roof end, apex, floor start) in the slit's cross-section plane.
//
// foldSlot(m, path, up, across, sections, width, taper, falloff, maxEdge, maxPasses, problems):
//   - 'path' is the line of the wedge's APEX, as it falls on the surface: the apex lies under it. 'sections' are three
//     RunCurves in the run fraction t of the path's own length (0 at its first point, 1 at its last): the apex DEPTH,
//     the ROOF's angle and the FLOOR's angle, in radians, each wall's angle from the opening's plane at the opening
//     (an angle over a right angle is an undercut wall: it leans back over the groove). 'width' is the farthest from
//     the path, along the surface, that a wall's foot may be; 'maxEdge' and 'maxPasses' are displaceRegion's.
//   - THE SECTION PLANES ('across'). The depth and the angles are measured in planes normal to 'across', the way the
//     front strip's cuts are taken in x-planes, not in planes square to the path. A vertex's STATION is the place
//     where its OWN plane (through the vertex, normal to 'across') meets the path, so the wall feet in that plane are
//     exactly the numbers measured there, however the path leans against the planes (square to the path they would
//     be 1 / cos(yaw) too wide). Parallel planes never cross, so no bend test is needed in this form. 'across' must
//     serve the whole path: every piece of it must advance along 'across' at an angle of at least 20 degrees from the
//     planes (its direction's component along 'across' at least sin 20 degrees = 0.342), and never turn back. A path
//     that does either (an arc turning more than 90 degrees against one 'across', a plane meeting the path twice) is
//     refused, with a problem line; an eyelid slit curving round the eye needs planes that turn, a later option.
//     'across' of (0, 0, 0) means planes SQUARE TO THE PATH at its nearest point, the first form of this function
//     (kept for a path with no one axis); there the bend test below applies.
//   - THE FRAME. 'up' is the opening's normal (the base normal at the opening), explicit: guessing it from the vertex
//     normals fails on a curved band whose opening is a small part. It is made square to 'across' (or, with an 'across'
//     of 0, square to the path's tangent T at each point). INTO is -up, the direction of the depth. The SIDE is
//     up x across (up x T). A vertex's offset 'a' is its distance from the path in its plane along the side (the roof is
//     on the positive side).
//   - THE WEDGE at run fraction t has its apex at 'depth' along INTO under the path (a = 0). The roof wall leaves the
//     apex up to the opening's plane at the roof's angle and meets it at a = depth / tan(roof) (its foot, on the roof's
//     side of the path; negative for an undercut wall); the floor wall at a = -depth / tan(floor). The OPENING is the
//     stretch of the plane between the two feet, floor foot to roof foot. Feet farther than 'width' from the path are held
//     to it, with a problem line.
//   - ASSIGNMENT AT THE APEX. The band, the opening, is split at its own middle: a vertex on the roof's side of it goes
//     to the roof wall, one on the other side to the floor wall, and each takes its place by arc length along its wall:
//     a vertex at fraction f of the way from the opening's edge to the middle goes to fraction f of the way from the
//     edge's foot to the apex. (Where the opening is centred on the path, as for a groove that is not undercut and is
//     symmetric, this is the path's own line.) The surface keeps its own curve and detail: the vertex moves by the
//     difference between where the wall puts it and where the plane had it, along the side and along INTO. A vertex at
//     or beyond a foot is not moved, so there is no step, and everything outside the opening is bit for bit the input.
//   - A CONTINUOUS OFFSET. Refinement splits an edge to halve it, and cannot close a jump between its two ends, so the
//     offset is continuous everywhere: (1) the depth must reach 0 at both ends of the path, or be tapered to 0 there
//     over 'taper' (a length along the path; a smooth fall; a problem line says the depth was changed); a depth above 0
//     at an end with 'taper' of 0 is refused; the fold is the identity where the depth is 0; (2) the part of the surface
//     that lies off the opening's plane (another part of the surface, over or under it) is folded with a weight that falls
//     smoothly from 1 at the plane to 0 at a distance of 'falloff' from it along 'up' (a smoothstep), not a cut-off.
//     A vertex whose plane meets the path beyond an end is not moved.
//   - BENDS (an 'across' of 0 only). Where the path bends so sharply that neighbouring cross-section planes (square to the
//     path at neighbouring points) meet within 'width' of the path, on the inside of the bend (the fanned muzzle cuts of
//     the design review): two neighbouring points a distance ds apart whose tangents turn by theta have planes that meet at
//     ds / theta from the path. On the inside the feet are held to that distance (the wall stays at its depth, so it is
//     steeper), and one problem line names the stations (the path's points) and the narrowest width used. If that is
//     below one edge length of the band's input (the mean of the edges that have an end in the opening) the call refuses.
//   - REFINEMENT is displaceRegion's, one driver (dsRun in heightpatch.cone): the region is the faces with a vertex in
//     the opening (not beyond the path's ends); every edge of it whose length AFTER the fold is over 'maxEdge' is split,
//     up to 'maxPasses' passes, the ring of faces beside split edges split to match, and a new vertex takes the fold at
//     its own place. Channels are carried as displaceRegion carries them.
//   - A REFUSAL is a problem line and an unchanged copy: a path of fewer than 2 points or with a piece of no length;
//     'width', 'maxEdge' or 'falloff' at or below 0 (or not a number); a negative 'taper'; an 'up' that is 0 or along
//     'across'; sections not 3 curves; a depth below 0 or not a number; a depth above 0 at an end of the path with no
//     'taper'; a taper over half the path; a wall's angle at or below 0 or at or over two right angles where the depth is
//     above 0; walls that cross at positive depth (the floor's foot beyond the roof's: the walls meet before the apex); an
//     'across' that cannot serve the path (above); a band limited below one edge. NO CALL IS A SILENT COPY: one that folds
//     no vertex (no vertex of the surface in reach of the path's opening, or none inside it) says so in a problem line.

struct SlotField {
  pts: List[Vec3];       // the path
  dist: List[f32];       // distance along the path to each point
  total: f32;
  tan: List[Vec3];       // per point: the unit tangent
  nrm: List[Vec3];       // per point: the opening's normal, unit and square to the tangent (across of 0)
  limPos: List[f32];     // per point: the farthest a foot on the positive side may be (width, or the bend's)
  limNeg: List[f32];     // per point: the same on the negative side
  tab: List[f32];        // depth, roof, floor, three to a sample, ts + 1 samples evenly in t
  ts: usize;
  width: f32;
  across: Vec3;          // unit, pointing the way the path advances; (0, 0, 0): planes square to the path
  up: Vec3;              // unit, square to across (when across is not 0)
  proj: List[f32];       // per point: its place along across (rising)
  taper: f32;
  falloff: f32;
}

struct SlotHit {
  k: usize;
  u: f32;
  q: Vec3;
  d2: f32;
  beyond: bool;          // the nearest point is an end of the path and the place is past it
}

// Where a place is against the wedge at its own station
struct SlotLocal {
  ok: bool;
  a: f32;                // its distance from the path along the side
  ar: f32;               // the roof foot
  af: f32;               // the floor foot
  depth: f32;
  down: Vec3;            // INTO, the direction of the depth
  side: Vec3;
  w: f32;                // the near-plane weight, 1 at the opening's plane to 0 at 'falloff' from it
}

fn slotNearest(f: &SlotField, p: Vec3) SlotHit {
  let n = f.pts.len();
  var best = SlotHit(0usize, 0., *f.pts[0usize], 3.0e38, false);
  var k = 0usize;
  while k + 1usize < n {
    let a = *f.pts[k];
    let seg = *f.pts[k + 1usize] - a;
    let l2 = seg.dot(seg);
    var raw: f32 = 0.;
    if l2 > 0. { raw = (p - a).dot(seg) / l2; }
    var u = raw;
    if u < 0. { u = 0.; }
    if u > 1. { u = 1.; }
    let q = a + seg * u;
    let d = p - q;
    let d2 = d.dot(d);
    if d2 < best.d2 {
      best = SlotHit(k, u, q, d2, (k == 0usize && raw < 0.) || (k + 2usize == n && raw > 1.));
    }
    k = k + 1usize;
  }
  best
}

// The place's station: where the plane through it, normal to across, meets the path; beyond when that is past an end
fn slotStation(f: &SlotField, p: Vec3) SlotHit {
  if !(f.across.dot(f.across) > 0.) { return slotNearest(f, p); }
  let n = f.pts.len();
  let c = p.dot(f.across);
  if c < *f.proj[0usize] || c > *f.proj[n - 1usize] { return SlotHit(0usize, 0., *f.pts[0usize], 0., true); }
  var lo = 0usize;
  var hi = n - 1usize;
  while hi - lo > 1usize {
    let mid = (lo + hi) / 2usize;
    if *f.proj[mid] <= c { lo = mid; } else { hi = mid; }
  }
  let s0 = *f.proj[lo];
  let s1 = *f.proj[lo + 1usize];
  var u = (c - s0) / (s1 - s0);
  if u < 0. { u = 0.; }
  if u > 1. { u = 1.; }
  let a = *f.pts[lo];
  SlotHit(lo, u, a + (*f.pts[lo + 1usize] - a) * u, 0., false)
}

fn slotTab(f: &SlotField, t: f32, c: usize) f32 {
  var x = t * f32.from(f.ts);
  if x < 0. { x = 0.; }
  var i = usize.from(libc.floorf(x));
  if i >= f.ts { i = f.ts - 1usize; }
  var fx = x - f32.from(i);
  if fx > 1. { fx = 1.; }
  *f.tab[3usize * i + c] * (1. - fx) + *f.tab[3usize * (i + 1usize) + c] * fx
}

// The roof's and floor's feet for depth d and the two angles, held to the limits lp (positive side) and ln (negative)
fn slotFoot(d: f32, ang: f32, sign: f32, lp: f32, ln: f32) f32 {
  var e = sign * d * ang.cos() / ang.sin();
  if e > lp { e = lp; }
  if e < -ln { e = -ln; }
  e
}

// The smoothstep of x held to [0, 1]
fn slotSmooth(x: f32) f32 {
  var e = x;
  if e < 0. { e = 0.; }
  if e > 1. { e = 1.; }
  e * e * (3. - 2. * e)
}

fn slotLocal(f: &SlotField, p: Vec3) SlotLocal {
  let none = SlotLocal(false, 0., 0., 0., 0., Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Vec3(0., 0., 0.), 0.);
  let h = slotStation(f, p);
  if h.beyond { return none; }
  let k = h.k;
  let u = h.u;
  var nn = f.up;
  var side = unit(nn.cross(f.across));
  if !(f.across.dot(f.across) > 0.) {
    let tn = unit(*f.tan[k] * (1. - u) + *f.tan[k + 1usize] * u);
    nn = *f.nrm[k] * (1. - u) + *f.nrm[k + 1usize] * u;
    nn = nn - tn * nn.dot(tn);
    if !(nn.dot(nn) > 0.) { return none; }
    nn = unit(nn);
    side = unit(nn.cross(tn));
  }
  let seg = (*f.pts[k + 1usize] - *f.pts[k]).length();
  var s = *f.dist[k] + u * seg;
  var t: f32 = 0.;
  if f.total > 0. { t = s / f.total; }
  var depth = slotTab(f, t, 0usize);
  if f.taper > 0. {
    var e = s;
    if f.total - s < e { e = f.total - s; }
    depth = depth * slotSmooth(e / f.taper);
  }
  if !(depth > 0.) { return none; }
  let lp = *f.limPos[k] * (1. - u) + *f.limPos[k + 1usize] * u;
  let ln = *f.limNeg[k] * (1. - u) + *f.limNeg[k + 1usize] * u;
  let ar = slotFoot(depth, slotTab(f, t, 1usize), 1., lp, ln);
  let af = slotFoot(depth, slotTab(f, t, 2usize), -1., lp, ln);
  if !(ar > af) { return none; }
  // The part of the surface off the opening's plane (over or under it, along the normal) is folded with a weight that
  // falls smoothly to 0 at 'falloff' from the plane
  let off = ((p - h.q).dot(nn)).abs();
  if !(off < f.falloff) { return none; }
  let w = slotSmooth(1. - off / f.falloff);
  SlotLocal(true, (p - h.q).dot(side), ar, af, depth, nn * (-1.), side, w)
}

// How far the fold moves the place p: the wall's place for the one the plane had, along the side and along INTO
fn slotOffset(f: &SlotField, p: Vec3) Vec3 {
  let zero = Vec3(0., 0., 0.);
  let l = slotLocal(f, p);
  if !l.ok { return zero; }
  if !(l.a < l.ar && l.a > l.af) { return zero; }
  let u = (l.ar - l.a) / (l.ar - l.af);
  var a2: f32 = 0.;
  var b2: f32 = 0.;
  if u <= 0.5 {
    let g = 2. * u;
    a2 = l.ar * (1. - g);
    b2 = l.depth * g;
  } else {
    let g = 2. * (1. - u);
    a2 = l.af * (1. - g);
    b2 = l.depth * g;
  }
  (l.side * (a2 - l.a) + l.down * b2) * l.w
}

// Whether the place is in the opening (a margin of 1e-4 of it, and 'margin' more) and not beyond the path's ends
fn slotInBand(f: &SlotField, p: Vec3, margin: f32) bool {
  let l = slotLocal(f, p);
  if !l.ok { return false; }
  let tol = 0.0001 * (l.ar - l.af) + 0.000001 + margin;
  l.a >= l.af - tol && l.a <= l.ar + tol
}

fn slotRefused(m: &PolyMesh, problems: &mut List[String], why: &str) PolyMesh {
  var s = String.from("foldSlot: ");
  s.append(why);
  problems.push(s);
  m.clone()
}

pub fn foldSlot(m: &PolyMesh, path: &Path, up: Vec3, across: Vec3, sections: &List[RunCurve], width: f32, taper: f32,
    falloff: f32, maxEdge: f32, maxPasses: u32, problems: &mut List[String]) PolyMesh {
  let np = path.points.len();
  if np < 2usize { return slotRefused(m, problems, "the path has fewer than 2 points"); }
  if !(width > 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "width is not above 0"); }
  if !(maxEdge > 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "maxEdge is not above 0"); }
  if !(falloff > 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "falloff is not above 0"); }
  if !(taper >= 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "taper is below 0 (or not a number)"); }
  if sections.len() != 3usize { return slotRefused(m, problems, "sections are not 3 curves (depth, roof, floor)"); }
  let dist = path.distances();
  let total = *dist[np - 1usize];
  if !(total > 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "the path has no length"); }
  if taper * 2. > total { return slotRefused(m, problems, "taper is over half the path"); }
  var i = 0usize;
  while i + 1usize < np {
    if !((*path.points[i + 1usize] - *path.points[i]).length() > 0.) {
      return slotRefused(m, problems, "the path has a piece of no length");
    }
    i = i + 1usize;
  }

  // The section planes: across, made to point the way the path advances, and every piece of the path must serve it
  let fixed = across.dot(across) > 0.;
  var ax = Vec3(0., 0., 0.);
  var upN = Vec3(0., 0., 0.);
  var proj = List[f32]();
  if fixed {
    ax = unit(across);
    if (*path.points[np - 1usize] - *path.points[0usize]).dot(ax) < 0. { ax = ax * (-1.); }
    let uq = up - ax * up.dot(ax);
    if !(uq.dot(uq) > 0.000001 * up.dot(up) && up.dot(up) > 0.) {
      return slotRefused(m, problems, "up is 0 or along across");
    }
    upN = unit(uq);
    i = 0usize;
    while i + 1usize < np {
      let seg = *path.points[i + 1usize] - *path.points[i];
      let c = seg.dot(ax) / seg.length();
      if !(c > 0.) {
        return slotRefused(m, problems, "across cannot serve the path: it turns back along across, so a plane meets it more than once");
      }
      if c < 0.3420201 {
        return slotRefused(m, problems, "across cannot serve the path: a piece of it lies within 20 degrees of the section planes");
      }
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
    i = 0usize;
    while i < np {
      proj.push((*path.points[i]).dot(ax));
      i = i + 1usize;
    }
  } else if !(up.dot(up) > 0.) {
    return slotRefused(m, problems, "up is 0");
  }

  // The sections, sampled: 16 to a path piece (at least 64), linear between samples
  var ts = 16usize * (np - 1usize);
  if ts < 64usize { ts = 64usize; }
  var tab = List[f32].withCapacity(3usize * (ts + 1usize));
  let twoRight: f32 = 3.1415927;
  var footCapped = false;
  i = 0usize;
  while i <= ts {
    let t = f32.from(i) / f32.from(ts);
    let d = sections[0usize].at(t);
    let roofA = sections[1usize].at(t);
    let floorA = sections[2usize].at(t);
    if !(d >= 0.) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "a depth is below 0 (or not a number)"); }
    if d > 0. {
      if !(roofA > 0.) || !(floorA > 0.) || !(roofA < twoRight) || !(floorA < twoRight) {
        return slotRefused(m, problems, "a wall's angle is not between 0 and two right angles");
      }
      let ar = d * roofA.cos() / roofA.sin();
      let af = -d * floorA.cos() / floorA.sin();
      if af > ar + 0.000001 { return slotRefused(m, problems, "the walls cross at positive depth (the floor's foot is beyond the roof's)"); }
      if ar > width || ar < -width || af > width || af < -width { footCapped = true; }
    }
    tab.push(d);
    tab.push(roofA);
    tab.push(floorA);
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  var tapered = false;
  if *tab[0usize] > 0.000001 || *tab[3usize * ts] > 0.000001 {
    if !(taper > 0.) {
      return slotRefused(m, problems, "the depth is above 0 at an end of the path and taper is 0: the offset would step there (give taper, or a depth curve that reaches 0 at both ends)");
    }
    tapered = true;
  }

  // The frame at each path point: the tangent and the opening's normal square to it (up)
  var tan = List[Vec3].withCapacity(np);
  var nrm = List[Vec3].withCapacity(np);
  i = 0usize;
  while i < np {
    let tg = path.tangentAt(i);
    let sq = up - tg * up.dot(tg);
    if !fixed && !(sq.dot(sq) > 0.000001 * up.dot(up)) { return slotRefused(m, problems, "up is along the path"); }
    tan.push(tg);
    nrm.push(unit(sq));
    i = i + 1usize;
  }
  var lim = SlotField(path.points.clone(), dist, total, tan, nrm, List[f32].withCapacity(np), List[f32].withCapacity(np),
    tab, ts, width, ax, upN, proj, taper, falloff);
  i = 0usize;
  while i < np {
    lim.limPos.push(width);
    lim.limNeg.push(width);
    i = i + 1usize;
  }

  let nv = m.vertexCount();
  var inBand = List[bool].withCapacity(nv);
  var v = 0usize;
  while v < nv {
    inBand.push(slotInBand(&lim, *m.positions[v], 0.));
    v = v + 1usize;
  }
  var nIn = 0usize;
  v = 0usize;
  while v < nv {
    if *inBand[v] { nIn = nIn + 1usize; }
    v = v + 1usize;
  }
  if nIn == 0usize {
    return slotRefused(m, problems, "no vertex of the surface lies in the opening (nothing is in reach of the path, or the depth is 0 there): nothing is folded");
  }

  // The edges with an end in the opening: their mean (the bend test), and the longest (the region's margin)
  var sumEdge: f64 = 0.0;
  var nEdge = 0usize;
  var reach: f32 = 0.;
  var e = 0usize;
  while e < m.edgeCount() {
    let ia = usize.from(m.fromVertex(2u32 * u32.from(e)));
    let ib = usize.from(m.toVertex(2u32 * u32.from(e)));
    if *inBand[ia] || *inBand[ib] {
      let le = (*m.positions[ia] - *m.positions[ib]).length();
      sumEdge = sumEdge + f64.from(le);
      nEdge = nEdge + 1usize;
      if le > reach { reach = le; }
    }
    e = e + 1usize;
  }
  let edge = f32.from(sumEdge / f64.from(nEdge));

  // Bends (an across of 0 only): the neighbouring planes meet at ds / theta from the path, on the inside
  if !fixed {
    var bendLo = np;
    var bendHi = 0usize;
    var narrow = width;
    var k = 0usize;
    while k + 1usize < np {
      let t0 = *lim.tan[k];
      let t1 = *lim.tan[k + 1usize];
      let ds = (*lim.pts[k + 1usize] - *lim.pts[k]).length();
      let theta = libc.atan2f(t0.cross(t1).length(), t0.dot(t1));
      if theta > 0.000001 && ds / theta < width {
        let rho = ds / theta;
        let nn = unit(*lim.nrm[k] + *lim.nrm[k + 1usize]);
        let tm = unit(t0 + t1);
        let side = unit(nn.cross(tm));
        let inside = (t1 - t0).dot(side) > 0.;
        var j = k;
        while j <= k + 1usize {
          if inside {
            if rho < *lim.limPos[j] { lim.limPos.set(j, rho); }
          } else {
            if rho < *lim.limNeg[j] { lim.limNeg.set(j, rho); }
          }
          j = j + 1usize;
        }
        if k < bendLo { bendLo = k; }
        if k + 1usize > bendHi { bendHi = k + 1usize; }
        if rho < narrow { narrow = rho; }
      }
      k = k + 1usize;
    }
    if bendHi > 0usize {
      if narrow < edge { return slotRefused(m, problems, "the bend limits the band below one edge of the input"); }
      var s = String.from("foldSlot: the path bends so sharply that neighbouring planes meet within width, at stations ");
      s.appendUInt(u64.from(bendLo));
      s.append(" to ");
      s.appendUInt(u64.from(bendHi));
      s.append("; the band is limited there to ");
      s.appendF32(narrow);
      s.append(" (width ");
      s.appendF32(width);
      s.append(")");
      problems.push(s);
    }
    v = 0usize;
    while v < nv {
      inBand.set(v, slotInBand(&lim, *m.positions[v], 0.));
      v = v + 1usize;
    }
  }

  // The region: the faces with a vertex in the opening; and a count of the vertices the fold moves
  var moves = 0usize;
  v = 0usize;
  while v < nv {
    if *inBand[v] {
      let o = slotOffset(&lim, *m.positions[v]);
      if o.dot(o) > 0. { moves = moves + 1usize; }
    }
    v = v + 1usize;
  }
  if moves == 0usize {
    return slotRefused(m, problems, "no vertex lies strictly inside the opening, so none is folded");
  }
  // The notes (after every refusal, so a refused call has one line)
  if tapered {
    problems.push(String.from("foldSlot: the depth is above 0 at an end of the path; it is tapered to 0 there over taper"));
  }
  if footCapped {
    problems.push(String.from("foldSlot: a wall's foot is farther than width from the path; it is held to width (the wall is steeper)"));
  }
  // The region is wider than the opening by the longest input edge in it: a face beside a split edge is split to match, and
  // its far side is never measured (heightpatch.cone), so the faces the fold reaches must all be region faces
  var wide = List[bool].withCapacity(nv);
  v = 0usize;
  while v < nv {
    wide.push(slotInBand(&lim, *m.positions[v], reach));
    v = v + 1usize;
  }
  var region = List[u32]();
  var f = 0usize;
  while f < m.faceCount() {
    let vs = m.faceVertices(u32.from(f));
    var hit = false;
    var j = 0usize;
    while j < vs.len() {
      if *wide[usize.from(*vs[j])] { hit = true; }
      j = j + 1usize;
    }
    if hit { region.push(u32.from(f)); }
    f = f + 1usize;
  }
  if region.len() == 0usize { return slotRefused(m, problems, "no face has a vertex in the opening: nothing is folded"); }
  var on = DsOnto(false, false, List[Footprint](), List[SurfaceIndex](), List[f32](), 0u32, 0u32, 0u32, List[SlotField]());
  on.slot.push(lim);
  let patch = HeightPatch(Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Vec3(0., 0., 0.), Vec3(0., 0., 1.), 0u32, 0u32, List[f32]());
  dsRun(m, region.view(), &patch, &mut on, &List[Vec3](), &List[f32](), maxEdge, maxPasses, problems)
}
